    {
      "text": "Within the Zscaler Admin Console, you can create and edit namespaces and tags. A namespace is a container used to organize and group related tags that have been defined within Private Access (ZPA). Namespaces allow you to reuse the same tag names and values and manage them according to different needs. When configuring a namespace, you can create and assign tags, and optionally define tag values. For a complete list of ranges and limits per feature, see Ranges & Limitations. To learn more, see About Tag Management for Defined Application Segments. To learn how to connect a namespace to an application segment, see Configuring Defined Application Segments."
    },
    {
      "text": "Predefined namespaces and tags cannot be edited or deleted."
    },
    {
